{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/afluent\/asyncsequences\/asynciteratorsequence"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Afluent"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AsyncIteratorSequence"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AsyncIteratorSequence"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Afluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Afluent\/SequenceOperators\/AsyncIteratorSequence.swift#L40","fileName":"AsyncIteratorSequence.swift"},"title":"AsyncSequences.AsyncIteratorSequence","externalID":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO0B16IteratorSequenceV","symbolKind":"struct","extendedModule":"Afluent"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent","doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"A single-pass async sequence over an iterator you already made: the async counterpart of the standard","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"library’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"IteratorSequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Afluent\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/Afluent\/Sci"],"title":"Conforms To"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/AsyncIteratorSequence","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncIteratorSequence","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncIteratorProtocol","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScI"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use it to subscribe to a subject before the code that consumes the subject runs. A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/PassthroughSubject","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"drops values sent while nobody is subscribed, and an operator such as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch(strategy:)"},{"text":" subscribes only when","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its consumer’s task starts iterating, so values sent in between are lost. Making the subject’s iterator first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"subscribes at once; wrapping it in an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncIteratorSequence"},{"text":" hands that subscription to any operator.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Example","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Example"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let events = PassthroughSubject<String>()","\/\/ Subscribes now: every value sent from here on is buffered for the batches below.","let batches = AsyncIteratorSequence(events.makeAsyncIterator())","    .batch(strategy: .count(2))","events.send(\"launch\")","events.send(\"login\")","events.send(completion: .finished)","","let consumer = Task {","    for try await batch in batches {","        print(batch) \/\/ Prints: [\"launch\", \"login\"]","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The subscription belongs to the wrapped iterator. A subject’s iterator subscribes when it is made and buffers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every value sent after that until it is read, without limit. It unsubscribes when the last copy of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iterator is released, whether or not it was ever iterated, and when a task waiting in its "},{"code":"next()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cancelled; values sent after either are not delivered to it. To read the subject again, make a new iterator."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The sequence is single-pass. Each ","type":"text"},{"code":"makeAsyncIterator()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" returns a copy of the wrapped iterator, so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value-type iterator starts over from where it was wrapped, and a reference-type one, such as a subject’s,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shares its elements among every iteration."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/AsyncIteratorSequence\/AsyncIterator"],"title":"Structures"},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/AsyncIteratorSequence\/init(_:)"],"title":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/AsyncIteratorSequence\/makeAsyncIterator()"],"title":"Instance Methods"},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Aliases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/AsyncIteratorSequence\/Element"],"title":"Type Aliases"},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/AsyncIteratorSequence\/AsyncSequence-Implementations","doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/AsyncIteratorSequence\/AsyncSequence-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations"}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent/AsyncSequences/AsyncIteratorSequence/AsyncSequence-Implementations":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/AsyncIteratorSequence\/AsyncSequence-Implementations","title":"AsyncSequence Implementations","role":"collectionGroup","url":"\/documentation\/afluent\/asyncsequences\/asynciteratorsequence\/asyncsequence-implementations","abstract":[]},"doc://Afluent/s8SendableP":{"title":"Swift.Sendable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/s8SendableP"},"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent/PassthroughSubject":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A subject that broadcasts values to multiple consumers without storing a current value."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Unlike "},{"code":"CurrentValueSubject","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"PassthroughSubject","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" does not retain the most recent value."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"This is an "},{"code":"AsyncSequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that allows multiple tasks to asynchronously consume values and mimics Combine’s PassthroughSubject."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PassthroughSubject","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/afluent\/passthroughsubject","title":"PassthroughSubject","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/PassthroughSubject","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PassthroughSubject","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent/AsyncSequences/AsyncIteratorSequence/AsyncIterator":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AsyncIterator"}],"type":"topic","title":"AsyncSequences.AsyncIteratorSequence.AsyncIterator","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AsyncIterator"}],"url":"\/documentation\/afluent\/asyncsequences\/asynciteratorsequence\/asynciterator","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/AsyncIteratorSequence\/AsyncIterator","abstract":[],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent","role":"collection","title":"Afluent","url":"\/documentation\/afluent","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent/AsyncSequences/AsyncIteratorSequence/Element":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Element"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/AsyncIteratorSequence\/Element","title":"AsyncSequences.AsyncIteratorSequence.Element","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/afluent\/asyncsequences\/asynciteratorsequence\/element","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Element"}],"abstract":[]},"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent/AsyncSequences/AsyncIteratorSequence":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/AsyncIteratorSequence","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/afluent\/asyncsequences\/asynciteratorsequence","abstract":[{"text":"A single-pass async sequence over an iterator you already made: the async counterpart of the standard","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"library’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IteratorSequence"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncIteratorSequence","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AsyncIteratorSequence","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"AsyncSequences.AsyncIteratorSequence","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Afluent/Sci":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"_Concurrency.AsyncSequence","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/Sci"},"doc://Afluent/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"title":"Swift.SendableMetatype","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/s16SendableMetatypeP"},"doc://Afl